:: Mostly Done [event sister_quest scene] {"position":"3525,1325","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "Good News?" (sister_mostlyDone). Most of her classes are done for the semester, so she can come in from Noon on.
   I don't want her spending those hours at my desk: she is to go round the office, talk to the staff, keep them company
   and bring everyone coffee. The overview meetings stay ours.
   The quest's set switches her weekday routine to sister_stage1_noon (Define Schedule), which also opens her Noon cells
   in the scheduler. Her rounds show up afterwards as micro events 28 to 31 ("Her rounds" in Define Events). */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[15].img>><</silent>>
Her text came in just before lunch: <i>meeting room when u have a sec?? GOOD news. probably good. mostly good</i>

When I open the door she's sitting cross-legged on the table with her laptop on her knees, and she spins it around to face me before I've even closed the door behind me. It's her college portal. A list of courses, and next to nearly every one of them, a green check mark.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Look. Look at all the green." },
{ who: $player, text: "You finished early?" },
{ who: $sister, text: "Most of it! Two finals I took early, one paper I handed in at three in the morning, the timestamp is very embarrassing, and the only thing left is one seminar that meets once a week in the evening and is honestly mostly vibes." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So I was thinking. I could come in at noon. Every day. Every weekday, I mean, I'm not insane." },
{ text: "She says it fast, and then she watches my face, the way she watched it from the edge of my bed when she pitched me the internship." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Think about it">>
Three more hours a day. That's more of her week than her college gets now, and she's holding it out to me like a present she wrapped herself. She'd spend every one of those hours at the corner of my desk if I let her. I have better uses for them.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Noon works. But you're not spending it at my desk." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I don't spend time at your desk." },
{ who: $player, text: "You've spent more time at my desk this month than I have." },
{ who: $sister, text: "That's a statistic. Statistics can say anything." },
{ who: $player, text: "Here's the problem. Everybody out there works hard, nobody talks to anybody, and the mood gets a little worse every week. Nobody's in charge of that." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And you want me to be in charge of... vibes." },
{ who: $player, text: "Morale. Go round. Talk to people, keep them company, bring them coffee. Learn how everybody takes it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "So I'm the office golden retriever." },
{ who: $player, text: "You're the reason people like coming in." },
{ text: "She tries not to let that one show on her face. It shows anyway, all the way up to her ears." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

Then it catches up with her. She looks down at the laptop, at all that green, and the grin slips a little.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Okay, but... if I'm out there with everybody all day..." },
{ who: $sister, text: "More time here was supposed to mean more time, you know. Here." },
{ who: $player, text: "The overview meetings stay. Those are ours." },
{ text: "She repeats 'ours' under her breath, as if she's checking the word for cracks. Then she closes the laptop." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

<<linkreplace "Brief her on the staff">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Fine. Then give me the cheat sheet. What do I even talk to $brian.name about? He talks to his soldering iron. I've heard him apologize to it." },
{ who: $player, text: "$brian.name gets nervous around people, and around you, very nervous. Don't make him look at you. Ask him about whatever's on his desk and let him explain it, and he'll be fine." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And $ethan.name?" },
{ who: $player, text: "$ethan.name wants an audience. Laugh at one joke in three, or he'll never get any work done." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And $darius.name?" },
{ text: "She asks that one to the lid of her laptop instead of to me." },
{ who: $player, text: "$darius.name wants somebody to notice how smart he is. Notice it. Don't overdo it." },
{ who: $sister, text: "I would never overdo it." },
{ who: $player, text: "You overdo everything." },
{ who: $sister, text: "That's called enthusiasm. It's literally on my evaluation form." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

She writes all three down in the journal, under a heading she underlines twice: <i>The Staff (Field Guide)</i>. Under $brian.name she adds a small drawing of a soldering iron with a speech bubble that says <i>sorry</i>.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $sister, text: "Starting tomorrow. Noon. I'm going to need a tray. A really nice tray." },
{ text: "She hops off the table and gets as far as the door before she turns around." },
{ who: $sister, text: "And I'm still bringing you yours first. That's not negotiable." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

On her way back to her desk she stops at $mom.callName's to tell her the news, and $mom.callName hugs her right across the desk, keyboard and all. Over her shoulder, $sister.callName finds me through the open meeting room door and grins.

<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterRelation" 2>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 1>>
<<ProfileLog $sister "Mostly Done" "Most of her classes are done for the semester, so she's at the office from noon on now. I told her to spend that time with the staff: talk to them, keep them company, bring everyone coffee. She looked disappointed until I told her the overview meetings stay ours.">>
<<NextQuest $sister>>
<<run Notification.show($sister.callName + " is at the office from Noon on now. Her Noon actions are open in the scheduler.", { type: Notification.INFORMATION })>>
<<ReturnFromEvent>>
<</linkreplace>>
<</linkreplace>>
